```

Now `attrs[i].pValue` is non-NULL, so `p11_rpc_buffer_get_attribute` calls the serializer with `attr->pValue` non-NULL. In `p11_rpc_buffer_get_attribute_array_value`, `value` is non-NULL, so it writes `count` CK_ATTRIBUTE structures into `attrs[i].pValue`. But `attrs[i].pValue` was allocated with only `length` bytes.

The check `decode_length > length` ensures `length >= count * sizeof(CK_ATTRIBUTE)`. So if `length == count * sizeof(CK_ATTRIBUTE)`, the allocation is exactly right. Hmm.

